.TH KALKYLARK 1 "November 2026" "Kalkylark 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kalkylark \- a VisiCalc-style spreadsheet for VT100 terminals
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kalkylark
.RB [ \-p
.IR phosphor ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR colours ]
.RI [ file ]
.br
.B kalkylark \-V
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kalkylark
is a small spreadsheet in the style of VisiCalc (1979).
The sheet has 63 columns
.RB ( A .. BK )
and 254 rows.
It needs only a VT100-compatible terminal; no curses library is used.
.PP
If
.I file
exists it is loaded; otherwise it becomes the name used by the first save.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p " phosphor"
Colour theme:
.BR plain " (default),"
.BR green ", " amber " or " white ,
after the monitor phosphors of the time.
.TP
.BI \-c " colours"
Colour depth:
.BR 16 ", " 256 " or " true .
Normally detected from
.B COLORTERM
and
.BR TERM .
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.SH SCREEN
The top line shows the current cell, its format and its contents, and at
the right the recalculation order and, after a circular reference,
.BR CIRC .
The second line holds prompts and messages, the third the text being typed.
.SH ENTERING CELLS
The first key decides the kind of entry: a digit or one of
.B "+ \- . ( @"
starts a
.IR value ;
anything else a
.IR label .
A leading
.B \(dq
forces a label.
Enter stores the entry, an arrow key stores it and moves, Esc cancels.
.PP
While typing a value, after an operator,
.B (
or
.BR , ,
the arrow keys
.I point
at a cell and insert its coordinate; typing
.B .
while pointing turns it into a range such as
.BR A1...A9 .
.SH FORMULAS
Operators
.B "+ \- * / ^"
are evaluated strictly from left to right, with no precedence, as in
VisiCalc:
.B 2+3*4
is 20.
Use parentheses.
.PP
References are written
.BR A1 .. BK254 ;
ranges
.BR A1...A9 ,
.BR A1.A9 ,
.B A1..A9
or
.BR A1:A9 .
Empty cells and labels count as 0.
.PP
Functions:
.BR @SUM ", " @MIN ", " @MAX ", " @COUNT ", " @AVERAGE
(lists of values and ranges),
.BI @NPV( rate , range )\fR,\fP
.BI @LOOKUP( x , range )\fR,\fP
.BR @ABS ", " @INT ", " @SQRT ", " @EXP ", " @LN ", " @LOG10 ,
.BR @SIN ", " @COS ", " @TAN ", " @ASIN ", " @ACOS ", " @ATAN ,
.BR @PI ", " @NA ", " @ERROR .
.B ERROR
takes precedence over
.BR NA ,
and both propagate.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B Arrows, PgUp, PgDn, Home
Move the cell cursor.
.TP
.B >
Go to a coordinate.
.TP
.B !
Recalculate.
.TP
.B /B
Blank the current cell.
.TP
.B /C
Clear the whole sheet.
.TP
.BI /F " f"
Format the current cell:
.B G
general,
.B I
integer,
.B $
two decimals,
.B L
left,
.B R
right,
.B *
bar graph,
.B D
back to the global format.
.TP
.BI /GF " f"
Set the global format.
.TP
.BI /GC " n"
Set the column width (3 to 40) for all columns.
.TP
.BI /GO " o"
Recalculation order:
.B C
by column (default) or
.B R
by row, one pass each, as in VisiCalc; or
.B N
natural order, as in Lotus 1-2-3, where each formula is computed after
the formulas it reads.
.TP
.B /SS
Save.
.TP
.B /SL
Load.
.TP
.B /SQY
Quit (asks again if there are unsaved changes).
.TP
.B Ctrl-L
Redraw.
.TP
.B Ctrl-C
Quit immediately.
.SH FILES
Sheets are plain text, one record per line:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# kalkylark 1
/GO N
/GC 9
/GF G
>A1:"Rent
>B1:/F$:9500
>B3:@SUM(B1...B2)
.fi
.RE
.PP
A save writes a temporary file and renames it over the old one.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KALKYLARK_PHOSPHOR
Default theme for
.BR \-p .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set and not empty, use the plain theme unless
.B \-p
is given.
.TP
.BR TERM ", " COLORTERM
Used to detect the colour depth.
.SH NOTES
Kalkylark is an independent implementation written from scratch.
It is not affiliated with, and contains no code from, Lotus Development
Corporation, IBM, Software Arts or VisiCorp.
VisiCalc is a trademark of its respective owner.
